WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:09.880 align:start position:0%
A fly buzzes past your face.
You don't even think. You just catch it.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.880 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:16.360 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Your friend knocks his coffee off the
table.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:20.320 align:start position:0%
The cup hasn't even started to fall
and your hand is already [music] under

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.320 align:start position:0%
it.

00:00:22.925 --> 00:00:26.680 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; How? How did you do that?

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:34.640 align:start position:0%
A normal human reacts in [music] about a
quarter of a second.

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:39.400 align:start position:0%
You react in two and a half hundredths.
So, what if your reaction time was

00:00:36.025 --> 00:00:39.400 align:start position:0%
[music] 10 times faster?

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:45.320 align:start position:0%
Here's how it works.
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:49.840 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Your eyes see, your brain decides, your
muscles move.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:54.000 align:start position:0%
Your brain got 10 times faster. [music]
Your muscles did not.

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:56.360 align:start position:0%
You can't move faster. You just start
earlier.

00:00:55.675 --> 00:01:00.915 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; The ruler test.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:03.720 align:start position:0%
A normal person lets it drop 30 cm.
[music]

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:06.360 align:start position:0%
You?
3 mm.

00:01:06.155 --> 00:01:10.640 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; That's

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.640 align:start position:0%
not humanly possible.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:21.840 align:start position:0%
To you, the whole world moves in slow
motion.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.840 align:start position:0%
A falling flower pot?

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:30.445 align:start position:0%
Caught.
&gt;&gt; Woah.

00:01:28.425 --> 00:01:30.445 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:38.680 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Your phone slips out of your pocket.
Caught. Somebody throws a ball at your

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.680 align:start position:0%
head.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:41.581 align:start position:0%
Caught that, too.
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:54.400 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; A car runs a red light.
Everyone else freezes.

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:54.400 align:start position:0%
You've already stepped back.

00:01:55.936 --> 00:02:01.120 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; Online games.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:05.761 align:start position:0%
While the other [music] players are
still seeing you, you've already aimed,

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:09.800 align:start position:0%
shot, and moved.
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:13.000 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; 30 wins in a row.
They think I'm cheating.

00:02:13.621 --> 00:02:18.680 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; But where it gets really crazy is

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:23.480 align:start position:0%
sports.
A table tennis smash crosses the table

00:02:21.481 --> 00:02:28.480 align:start position:0%
[music] in a fifth of a second. Normal
players guess. You don't.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:31.280 align:start position:0%
You watch the ball leave the paddle, and
you're already there.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:41.520 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; 21 to 0.
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.520 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Who is this kid?

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:49.720 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Baseball.
A 160 km fastball reaches the plate in

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:52.840 align:start position:0%
4/10 of a second. [music]
Pros have to decide before it's halfway

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:58.560 align:start position:0%
there.
You watch it the whole way,

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.560 align:start position:0%
and crush it.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.767 align:start position:0%
Boxing. [music]

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:08.320 align:start position:0%
You see every punch coming.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:12.320 align:start position:0%
Nobody [music] can touch you.

00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:23.239 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; Okay.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:23.239 align:start position:0%
I give up.

00:03:23.707 --> 00:03:25.727 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:34.519 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; But the sport that changes [music] your
life is football.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:38.480 align:start position:0%
A penalty reaches the goal in under half
a second.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:43.519 align:start position:0%
Normal keepers guess a side.
You wait, watch the ball,

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:47.840 align:start position:0%
and go.
A perfect shot into the top corner is

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:52.320 align:start position:0%
still out of reach.
Everything else, saved.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:57.120 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Nine out of 10.
Pack your bags. [music] You're going to

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:57.120 align:start position:0%
the national team.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:06.200 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; 11 games, not a single [music] goal
conceded. Fans are calling him the wall.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:09.520 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Nobody is that fast without cheating.
So, they test you.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:13.480 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; No drugs. [music]
No tricks.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:17.200 align:start position:0%
His brain is just faster.
&gt;&gt; They even try you in the 100-m sprint.

00:04:16.762 --> 00:04:20.640 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; Bam!

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:22.240 align:start position:0%
You're gone before anyone else moves.
False start.

00:04:22.002 --> 00:04:27.480 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; Disqualified. It's a real rule.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:32.480 align:start position:0%
React faster than a tenth of a second,
and they decide you must have guessed.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:36.440 align:start position:0%
And there's a cost.
The [music] world feels slow.

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:37.600 align:start position:0%
Movies feel like slideshows.
Headaches.

00:04:37.068 --> 00:04:41.480 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; Endless hunger.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:45.760 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; You're bored again, aren't you?
&gt;&gt; Everything's just so [music]

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.760 align:start position:0%
slow.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:55.408 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Two years later, the World Cup final.
120 minutes, still zero to zero.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:58.000 align:start position:0%
Penalties.
&gt;&gt; [music]

00:04:55.520 --> 00:05:02.000 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Save. Save.
Goal. Top corner. Nobody could stop it.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:06.080 align:start position:0%
Save [music] again.
One last kick.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:08.480 align:start position:0%
Save it, and your country wins the World
Cup.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:15.120 align:start position:0%
The striker runs up.
And in that same moment, you see

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:20.800 align:start position:0%
something nobody else sees.
The cable holding the TV camera snaps.

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:25.280 align:start position:0%
Right below it, the ball boy.
&gt;&gt; Huh?

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:29.400 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Half a second.
You're the only person in the stadium

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:33.560 align:start position:0%
with time to choose.
The ball

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:33.560 align:start position:0%
or the boy?

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:48.240 align:start position:0%
Behind you, the ball rolls into the
empty net.

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:53.840 align:start position:0%
You just lost the World Cup final.
80,000 people go silent.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:57.920 align:start position:0%
Then the replay [music] comes up on a
giant screen.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:06:00.309 align:start position:0%
And one by one, they stand up and start
clapping. [music]

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:07.160 align:start position:0%
Mate,
you just won something bigger.

00:06:10.079 --> 00:06:14.840 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; He lost the World Cup, but he saved a

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:18.800 align:start position:0%
life.
Tonight the whole world is about [music]

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:21.440 align:start position:0%
the goalkeeper who chose a boy over a
trophy.

00:06:22.524 --> 00:06:27.640 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; So, you lost the final. There's a World

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:30.320 align:start position:0%
Cup every 4 years. There's only one of
that kid.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:36.120 align:start position:0%
3 days later, a long black car stops
outside your house.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:44.560 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; We'd been watching you.
How would you like to test your reflexes

00:06:42.160 --> 00:06:48.919 align:start position:0%
on something a lot faster than a
football?

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:50.520 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; Faster than a football? Like what?
&gt;&gt; Get in the car.

00:06:50.034 --> 00:06:54.600 align:start position:0%
&gt;&gt; [music]
&gt;&gt; And with a brain 10 times faster, you'd

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:58.604 align:start position:0%
